hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16233","He said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Jami ibn Abi Rashid and Asim from Abu Wail from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to be called brokers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he came to us at al-Baqi and said: O company of merchants, and he named us with a name better than our name: Selling is attended by oaths and lying, so mix it with charity."
"16234","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us from Abu Wail from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to buy awsaq in Madinah and we used to be called brokers. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and named us with a name better than what we named ourselves, and said: O company of merchants, this selling is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity."
"16235","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Mughirah from Abu Wail from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while we were in the market and said: This market is mixed with idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity."
"16236","He said: Bahz narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, he said: I heard Abu Wail narrating from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were selling slaves, called brokers, and said: O company of merchants, this selling of yours is mixed with idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity, or with something of charity."
"16237","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Sufyan from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Abu Wail from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to sell slaves in the market and we were called brokers, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named us with better than what we named ourselves, and said: O company of merchants, this selling is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity."
"16238","He said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Al-Amash narrated to us from Shaqiq from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to be called brokers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us and named us with a name better than it, and said: O company of merchants, this selling is attended by idle talk and oaths, so mix it with charity."
"16239","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, he said: Ibrahim, the freedman of Sukhayr, narrated to me from some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to forbid a sale, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, they are our livelihoods. He said: Then he said: No deception then. And we were called brokers, then he mentioned the hadith."
